<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mansur Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1545</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mansur Khan was a Chagatai khan of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moghulistan">Moghulistan</a> who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turfan">Turpan</a> in the first half of the 16th century. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-alaq">Sultan Ahmad Khan</a>, he waged repeated wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hami">Hami</a> and campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirats</a>. Under his rule the conversion of the Turpan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghurs</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> was largely completed.</p></div>
